<div class="mp-proj mk-bw" id="mk-proj-bollywood" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="mk-title-bollywood" hidden>
    <div class="mk-deck" role="group" aria-roledescription="slideshow" aria-label="Same Fame, Different Fates slides">
        <div class="mk-stage">
            <div class="mk-slide b-cover" data-title="Same fame">
                <video class="b-bg" data-src="/videos/projects/bollywood-cover.mp4" preload="none" poster="/videos/projects/bollywood-cover.jpg" muted loop playsinline autoplay aria-label="Three dressing-room mirrors on a vanity shelf, each framing a photo of its founder. Kay Beauty’s, with Katrina Kaif, stays lit as its revenue counts to 211.65 crore. Anomaly’s, with Priyanka Chopra Jonas, settles to a steady glow and is sold. 82°E’s, with Deepika Padukone, fades to grey as its bulbs go out and its revenue lands at 14.66 crore."></video>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">bollywood beauty case study, 2026</p>
                <h4 class="b-title">Same fame,<br /><em>different fates.</em></h4>
                <p class="b-lede">Three A-list actresses launched beauty brands. One grew, one was sold, one is shrinking. Why?</p>
                <p class="b-src">Photos via Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 3.0: Katrina Kaif and Priyanka Chopra Jonas by Bollywood Hungama; Deepika Padukone from Narendra Modi’s YouTube channel.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="The answer" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">the answer first</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">It wasn’t the star. <em>It was the structure and the story.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <div class="b-three b-ans">
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:0"><small class="b-lab">Same fame</small><b>Three A-listers, three launches</b><p>Katrina Kaif, Priyanka Chopra Jonas and Deepika Padukone were all at the top of Bollywood when their brands began.</p></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:1"><small class="b-lab">Different fates</small><b>A winner, an exit, a loser</b><p>Kay made ₹211.65 cr in FY26 at a profit. Anomaly was sold to Reliance. 82°E fell to ₹14.66 cr at a loss.</p></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:2"><small class="b-lab">The difference</small><b>A partner, a price, a name, a story</b><p>Kay had all four. Anomaly had a story and a fair price. 82°E had none of them.</p></div>
                </div>
                <p class="b-src">Source: Nykaa FY26 annual report (Form AOC-1); 82°E MCA filings via MediaNama; Reliance Retail filing, 30 Apr 2026.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Three bets" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">the setup</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">Three stars made <em>three different bets.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <div class="b-three b-bet">
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--c:var(--kay);--n:0"><h5>Kay Beauty</h5><dl>
                        <dt>Founder</dt><dd>Katrina Kaif</dd><dt>Launched</dt><dd>Oct 2019, makeup</dd>
                        <dt>Partner</dt><dd>Nykaa, as 51% owner and retailer</dd><dt>Hero price</dt><dd>Lipstick ₹999</dd>
                        <dt>Sold on</dt><dd>Nykaa app and stores, UAE, UK</dd><dt>Her stake</dt><dd>41.5%</dd><dt>Name owned by</dt><dd>The Kay company</dd></dl></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--c:var(--ano);--n:1"><h5>Anomaly</h5><dl>
                        <dt>Founder</dt><dd>Priyanka Chopra Jonas</dd><dt>Launched</dt><dd>Feb 2021, haircare</dd>
                        <dt>Partner</dt><dd>Maesa, a US brand incubator</dd><dt>Hero price</dt><dd>Shampoo $5.99</dd>
                        <dt>Sold on</dt><dd>Target, Walmart, CVS, then Nykaa</dd><dt>Her stake</dt><dd>Never disclosed</dd><dt>Name owned by</dt><dd>Maesa, now Reliance</dd></dl></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--c:var(--e82);--n:2"><h5>82°E</h5><dl>
                        <dt>Founder</dt><dd>Deepika Padukone</dd><dt>Launched</dt><dd>Nov 2022, skincare</dd>
                        <dt>Partner</dt><dd>None: a $7.5M seed round</dd><dt>Hero price</dt><dd>Moisturiser ₹2,700</dd>
                        <dt>Sold on</dt><dd>Its own website only</dd><dt>Her stake</dt><dd>About 15%, with Ranveer</dd><dt>Name owned by</dt><dd>Her family office</dd></dl></div>
                </div>
                <p class="b-src">Source: launch announcements; company registry data (Mar 2026); Storyboard18 (Apr 2026); IP India; USPTO; Reliance Retail filing.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Revenue" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">the money</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">Kay grew 14x in six years. <em>82°E shrank in year two.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <div class="b-key"><span><i style="--c:var(--kay)"></i>Kay Beauty</span><span><i style="--c:var(--e82)"></i>82°E</span><span>Audited revenue, ₹ crore. Anomaly never disclosed revenue before it was sold.</span></div>
                <div style="margin-top:auto;display:grid;gap:0.6cqw">
                    <div class="b-cols" role="img" aria-label="Audited revenue in crore. Kay Beauty: FY20 14.94, FY21 23.14, FY22 27.56, FY23 60.56, FY24 88.24, FY25 131.76, FY26 211.65. 82°E: FY24 21.21, FY25 14.66.">
                        @for (var i = 0; i < years.Length; i++)
                        {
                            <div class="b-yr">
                                @if (kayRev[i] is double k)
                                {
                                    <i style="--c:var(--kay);--h:@(F(Math.Round(k / revMax * 100, 1)))%;--d:@(F(i * 0.08))s"><b>@F(Math.Round(k, 0))</b></i>
                                }
                                @if (e82Rev[i] is double e)
                                {
                                    <i style="--c:var(--e82);--h:@(F(Math.Round(e / revMax * 100, 1)))%;--d:@(F(i * 0.08 + 0.3))s"><b>@F(Math.Round(e, 0))</b></i>
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                    <div class="b-yrs">@foreach (var y in years) { <span>@y</span> }</div>
                </div>
                <p class="b-src">Source: CRISIL rating notes (FY20, FY21); Nykaa FY26 annual report, Form AOC-1 (FY22 to FY26); 82°E MCA filings via MediaNama and TechStory.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Profit" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">the bottom line</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">Kay made money every year. <em>82°E lost more than it sold.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <div class="b-three" style="margin-top:auto">
                    <div class="b-card b-stat b-anim" style="--c:var(--kay);--n:0"><b>₹55.6 cr</b><span>Kay’s total profit, FY20 to FY26: seven profitable years in a row</span></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-stat b-anim" style="--c:var(--ano);--n:1"><b>Sold</b><span>Anomaly’s owner sold the brand to Reliance Retail in April 2026 without ever reporting its numbers</span></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-stat b-anim" style="--c:var(--e82);--n:2"><b>₹35.7 cr</b><span>82°E’s losses in FY24 and FY25 alone, on ₹35.9 cr of revenue</span></div>
                </div>
                <p class="b-lede" style="margin-top:1cqw">Kay’s FY26 profit was ₹21.8 cr, about double FY25. 82°E spent ₹1.77 to earn every ₹1 in FY25, and its net worth turned negative.</p>
                <p class="b-src">Source: Nykaa FY26 annual report; CRISIL; 82°E MCA filings via MediaNama, TechStory and Tofler; Reliance Retail filing.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="The partner" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">structure 01, the partner</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">85% of Kay’s sales go <em>to its own co-owner.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <p class="b-lede">Nykaa owns 51% of Kay, stocks it on its app and in its stores, and collects an 8% royalty on every rupee. Kay never had to win a retailer. Anomaly rented shelf space at Target. 82°E sold only on its own website.</p>
                <div style="margin-top:auto;display:grid;gap:0.8cqw">
                    <p class="b-cap">Who bought Kay’s stock, FY26 revenue of ₹211.65 cr</p>
                    <div class="b-split" role="img" aria-label="Nykaa E-Retail 111.4 crore, FSN Brands Marketing 61.4 crore, FSN International 8.3 crore, all other buyers 30.6 crore.">
                        <div style="flex:111.4;background:var(--b-wine);color:#F8F2EA;--d:0s"><b>₹111.4 cr</b><span>Nykaa online</span></div>
                        <div style="flex:61.4;background:#9A4A5A;color:#F8F2EA;--d:0.3s"><b>₹61.4 cr</b><span>Nykaa stores and trade</span></div>
                        <div style="flex:8.3;background:#C99AA2;--d:0.6s"></div>
                        <div style="flex:30.6;background:var(--peer);color:var(--b-ink);--d:0.9s"><b>₹30.6 cr</b><span>everyone else</span></div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="b-cap" style="text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0">The thin band is Nykaa’s international arm, ₹8.3 cr.</p>
                </div>
                <p class="b-src">Source: Nykaa half-yearly related-party transaction filings, H1 and H2 FY26 (NSE); the 85% share is my calculation from them.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Marketing" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">structure 02, the cost of a customer</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">82°E paid for every customer. <em>Kay’s came with the shelf.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <p class="b-cap">Marketing spend as a share of revenue</p>
                <ul class="b-hbars" style="margin-top:auto" role="img" aria-label="Marketing as a percent of revenue: 82°E FY24 93 percent, Sugar 41, Honasa 36, Minimalist 30, 82°E FY25 30, Kay Beauty FY25 12.5.">
                    @{ var n = 0; }
                    @foreach (var m in mkt)
                    {
                        <li class="@(m.Cls == "peer" ? "" : "me")"><span>@m.Name</span><div class="t"><i style="--c:var(--@m.Cls);--w:@(F(m.Pct * 0.85))%;--n:@(n++)"></i><b style="--w:@(F(m.Pct * 0.85))%">@F(m.Pct)%</b></div></li>
                    }
                </ul>
                <p class="b-src">Source: audited filings for Kay and 82°E (82°E spent ₹19.65 cr on ₹21.21 cr of revenue in FY24, then cut marketing 78% and revenue fell 30%); peer ratios from a secondary analysis of their filings.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Price" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">structure 03, the price</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">82°E priced like Kiehl’s. <em>Kay priced like a treat.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <div class="b-two" style="grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr">
                    <div style="display:grid;gap:1cqw">
                        <p class="b-cap">Face moisturiser, list price per 10 ml</p>
                        <ul class="b-hbars" role="img" aria-label="Moisturiser price per 10 ml: Clinique 710 rupees, Kiehl's 680, 82°E 540, Kay 260, Minimalist 120, Hyphen 90.">
                            @{ var p = 0; }
                            @foreach (var x in moist)
                            {
                                <li class="@(x.Cls == "peer" ? "" : "me")"><span>@x.Name</span><div class="t"><i style="--c:var(--@x.Cls);--w:@(F(Math.Round(x.Price / 710.0 * 78, 1)))%;--n:@(p++)"></i><b style="--w:@(F(Math.Round(x.Price / 710.0 * 78, 1)))%">₹@x.Price</b></div></li>
                            }
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div style="display:grid;gap:1cqw">
                        <div class="b-card b-stat b-anim" style="--c:var(--e82);--n:0"><b>₹2,700</b><span>82°E’s moisturiser at launch in 2022, and still today. It discounts with Buy 1 Get 1, never by cutting the price.</span></div>
                        <div class="b-card b-stat b-anim" style="--c:var(--ano);--n:1"><b>$5.99</b><span>every Anomaly product at Target. A bargain in the US, though the same bottle cost 1.3x more in India.</span></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="b-src">Source: brand stores and retailer listings, 11 Oct 2026; launch prices via the Wayback Machine. Kay’s lipstick costs 1.3x Lakmé and 0.6x Sugar per gram.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="The name" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">structure 04, the name</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">A name you can say <em>is a name you can search.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <div class="b-three b-names" role="img" aria-label="Google search interest in India, yearly average 2019 to 2026 on one scale. Kay Beauty rises every year to 11.4. Anomaly stays near 1. 82°E peaks at 1.9 in 2023 and falls to 0.">
                    @foreach (var (word, cls, verdict, why, vals) in new[] {
                        ("Kay", "kay", "Easy", "One syllable and her own initial, like Fenty, Rare and Rhode.", tKay),
                        ("Anomaly", "ano", "A real word", "It means something (“all of us are anomalies”), but it is common, and a big New York ad agency has the same name.", tAno),
                        ("82°E", "e82", "Hard", "A number and a degree sign nobody can type. Search “82E” and you get unrelated results.", tE82) })
                    {
                        <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--c:var(--@cls)">
                            <span class="b-word">@word</span>
                            <p><b>@verdict:</b> @why</p>
                            <div class="b-spark">@for (var i = 0; i < vals.Length; i++) { <i style="--c:var(--@cls);--h:@(F(Math.Round(vals[i] / 11.4 * 100, 1)))%;--n:@i"></i> }</div>
                            <div class="b-ax"><span>2019</span><span>searches in India</span><span>2026</span></div>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
                <p class="b-src">Source: Google Trends, India, yearly average of monthly data on one shared scale, pulled 11 Oct 2026. Searches for “82°E” fall to zero after 2024, partly because people stop typing the symbol.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="The story" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">structure 05, the story</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">Kay and Anomaly told a story. <em>82°E told a coordinate.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <div class="b-three b-story">
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--c:var(--kay);--n:0"><small class="b-lab">Kay Beauty</small><q>It’s Kay to Be You</q><p><b>The story:</b> an actress who spent years under film lights wanted glam makeup that was kind to her skin. “Kay” is “okay” and her initial at once.</p><p><b>The feeling:</b> permission to be yourself, in full glam</p></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--c:var(--ano);--n:1"><small class="b-lab">Anomaly</small><q>All of us are anomalies</q><p><b>The story:</b> her hair was damaged by daily heat styling on set, and she grew up on her mother’s homemade hair masks. In India, “this brand was born here, and now it’s coming home.”</p><p><b>The feeling:</b> nobody gets to decide what’s standard</p></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--c:var(--e82);--n:2"><small class="b-lab">82°E</small><q>Self-Care Simplified</q><p><b>The story:</b> the longitude line that sets India’s clock. A place on a map, not a person or a problem.</p><p><b>The feeling:</b> unclear. On launch day a critic asked if it was “beauty or self-care”.</p></div>
                </div>
                <p class="b-src">Source: afaqs (Oct 2019, Aug 2022); WWD and NewBeauty (2021); 82e.com; The Established (Nov 2022).</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Why 82°E lost" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">the loser, up close</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">82°E’s fame couldn’t fix <em>a name, a price and a blur.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <div class="b-why">
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:0"><em>01</em><b>The name</b><p>A degree sign people can’t type or search, with a meaning that has to be explained</p></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:1"><em>02</em><b>The price</b><p>₹2,700 for 50 ml, about 4.5x Minimalist per ml, and never cut</p></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:2"><em>03</em><b>The branding</b><p>“Self-Care Simplified” never said what it does. Trade press called it “diffused” by 2026.</p></div>
                </div>
                <ul class="b-more">
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:3"><b>Two products</b> at launch, against Kay’s 48</li>
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:4"><b>Own website only:</b> no Nykaa, no Amazon, no stores</li>
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:5"><b>“Clinically tested”</b> meant surveys of 48 women</li>
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:6"><b>Lost a court case:</b> “Lotus Splash” barred, Feb 2026</li>
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:7"><b>Co-founder</b> left his full-time role in 2025</li>
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:8"><b>Fans tired</b> of back-to-back promos on her feed</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="b-src">Source: 82e.com; launch press kit (study footnotes); Business Today (Nov 2022); Storyboard18 (Apr 2026); LiveLaw (Feb 2026); IBTimes (Feb 2025).</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Scorecard" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">putting it together</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">Kay checked every box. <em>82°E checked almost none.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <table class="b-score">
                    <thead><tr><th>What it takes</th><th>Kay Beauty</th><th>Anomaly</th><th>82°E</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td>An A-list founder</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>A name you can say and search</td><td class="y">Yes, “Kay”</td><td class="p">Partly, a common word</td><td>No, a degree sign</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>A story people can retell</td><td class="y">Yes, “It’s Kay to Be You”</td><td class="y">Yes, “all of us are anomalies”</td><td>No, a map line</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Price fits the promise</td><td class="y">Yes, mid-priced</td><td class="p">Partly, $5.99 in the US only</td><td>No, Kiehl’s prices</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>A partner that also sells it</td><td class="y">Yes, Nykaa</td><td class="p">Partly, Maesa and Target</td><td>No, own site only</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Cheap to reach customers</td><td class="y">Yes, 12.5% on marketing</td><td>Never disclosed</td><td>No, 93% in FY24</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>A category where faces sell</td><td class="y">Yes, makeup</td><td>No, haircare</td><td>No, skincare</td></tr>
                        <tr class="out"><td>Result</td><td>₹211.65 cr revenue, ₹21.8 cr profit</td><td>Sold to Reliance, 2026</td><td>₹14.66 cr revenue, ₹12.26 cr loss</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
                <p class="b-src">Yes, Partly and No are my reading of the evidence on the slides before; every figure is sourced there.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide b-end" data-title="The takeaway" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">the takeaway</p>
                <h4 class="b-title">Fame gets a brand launched. <em>Structure and story decide if it lasts.</em></h4>
                <ul class="b-rules">
                    <li class="b-anim" style="--n:0"><b>Partner with the shelf</b>Co-own the brand with whoever sells it</li>
                    <li class="b-anim" style="--n:1"><b>Price for fans, not fame</b>A star’s name can’t carry a luxury price</li>
                    <li class="b-anim" style="--n:2"><b>An easy name, a real story</b>One word anyone can say, one story anyone can retell</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="b-lede b-anim" style="--n:3"><b>The catch:</b> much of what Kay had came from Nykaa, not from Katrina. It sells 85% of its stock to Nykaa and pays Nykaa 8% of every rupee. The lesson for the next A-lister isn’t to be more famous. It’s to choose the right partner.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mk-nav-row">
            <button type="button" class="mk-step prev" data-go="-1" aria-label="Previous slide">‹</button>
            <div class="mk-chapters" role="group" aria-label="Jump to a slide"></div>
            <button type="button" class="mk-step next" data-go="1" aria-label="Next slide">›</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mk-info">
        <div>
            <h3 id="mk-title-bollywood">Same Fame, Different Fates</h3>
            <p class="mp-proof-sub">Katrina Kaif, Priyanka Chopra Jonas and Deepika Padukone each launched a beauty brand. One grew, one was sold, one is shrinking. My case study of why, measured in audited revenue and profit.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="mp-proof-list">
            <li>Pulled Kay Beauty’s audited FY26 results (₹211.65 cr revenue, ₹21.8 cr profit) from Nykaa’s annual report before the press reported them</li>
            <li>Traced 85% of Kay’s sales to Nykaa companies through stock-exchange related-party filings</li>
            <li>Priced 89 products per 10 ml, pulled eight years of Google search data, and debunked a viral $542.7M Anomaly revenue claim</li>
            <li>Showed why 82°E lost: a name nobody can search, a luxury price and a brand with no story</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<script>
    // The cover video plays only while its slide and deck are open
    (() => {
        const vids = [...document.querySelectorAll('.mk-bw video')];
        if (matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) { vids.forEach(v => { v.removeAttribute('autoplay'); v.pause(); }); return; }
        setInterval(() => vids.forEach(v => {
            const open = !v.closest('.mk-slide').hidden && !v.closest('.mp-proj').hidden;
            if (open && v.paused) v.play().catch(() => {}); else if (!open && !v.paused) v.pause();
        }), 500);
    })();
</script>
